## Rule 2 — Data Separation

Keep the **sharp data fetching logic** strictly separated from the **recreational
data fetching logic**.

- Sharp data (Pinnacle) must be fetched via a dedicated EU-region API call
  filtered to `pinnacle` only.
- Recreational data (DraftKings, FanDuel, BetMGM, Caesars, bet365) must be
  fetched via a separate US-region API call.
- Do NOT mix sharp and recreational bookmakers in the same API request when
  the goal is to isolate the sharp baseline.
- **Overtime Markets / AMM data must NEVER be used as the sharp baseline.**
  AMM liquidity slippage causes prices to diverge from true market efficiency,
  which will break the EV math.

